97	## Static capability classes are the backend default
98	
99	Most backend modules are collections of functions. A static capability class
100	keeps that allocation-free shape while adding inheritance, `super`, and a
101	replaceable class address. The experimental `Static()` adapter makes its
102	methods safe to retain as callbacks:
103	
104	```ts
105	import { Static } from './Static';
106	
107	class $Users {
108	  static find(userId: string) {
109	    return database.users.find(userId);
110	  }
111	}
112	
113	export namespace Users {
114	  export const $Class = $Users;
115	  export let Class = Static($Class);
116	}
